# CODEOWNERS — who is automatically asked to review what.
#
# THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO DEFAULT OWNER LINE. A `*  @phuriphatma` rule would
# route every pull request to one person, which is the bottleneck this file
# exists to remove. Anything not listed here still needs one approving review
# (branch protection), but from ANY collaborator.
#
# Listed here = the load-bearing surfaces, taken from the "touch zones" table in
# CONTRIBUTING.md. Every one of them has cost this repo a real outage or a real
# bug; the write-ups are in docs/mistakes/.
#
# NOTE: this file makes GitHub REQUEST a review. It only BLOCKS a merge once
# `require_code_owner_reviews` is enabled on the branch protection rule — see
# docs/TEAM-WORKFLOW.md §8a.

# Auth, the Supabase client, and anything that talks to the database
/src/js/auth.js        @phuriphatma
/src/js/db.js          @phuriphatma

# Notifications and uploads — wrong here is a silent production outage
/src/js/notify.js      @phuriphatma
/src/js/uploads.js     @phuriphatma

# Schema is the source of truth for the live database
/supabase/             @phuriphatma

# Deploy plumbing, the notify service, nginx
/server/               @phuriphatma

# Apps Script — Discord webhooks live here; a redeploy hits production at once
/appscript/            @phuriphatma

# Proof scripts and migration tooling
/tools/                @phuriphatma

# CI, and this file
/.github/              @phuriphatma

# Agent context: charged to every session on the team, byte-capped
/CLAUDE.md             @phuriphatma
/.claude/              @phuriphatma

# The handoff
/STATE.md              @phuriphatma

